# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this React + Vite project following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart.

## Changes Made

### 1. Installed @vercel/analytics Package
- Added `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 to project dependencies
- Used npm to install the package (matching the project's package manager)
- Updated package-lock.json to reflect the new dependency

### 2. Integrated Analytics Component
Modified `/web/src/App.jsx`:
- Added import: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/react'`
- Added `<Analytics />` component to both return paths:
  - Added to the admin mode viewport (wrapped in fragment)
  - Added to the normal game view (wrapped in fragment)
- Used React fragments (`<>...</>`) to avoid adding extra DOM elements

### 3. Framework-Specific Implementation
This project uses React with Vite, so I followed the React/Create React App instructions from the official documentation:
- Used `@vercel/analytics/react` import path (React-specific)
- Added the `<Analytics />` component at the root level of the App component
- Preserved all existing code structure and functionality

### 4. Verification Steps Completed
✅ Build test passed - Project builds successfully with no errors
✅ Linter check - No new linting errors introduced by Analytics integration
✅ Dependencies updated - package.json and package-lock.json properly updated
✅ Code review - All changes maintain existing code patterns and structure

## Files Modified
- `/web/package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `/web/package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency tree
- `/web/src/App.jsx` - Added Analytics import and component

## Next Steps
After deployment to Vercel:
1. Enable Analytics in the Vercel dashboard for this project
2. Analytics will start tracking page views automatically
3. Data will be available in the Vercel Analytics dashboard after users visit the site
4. Monitor browser network requests for `/_vercel/insights/*` to verify proper integration

## Implementation Notes
- The Analytics component is lightweight and won't impact performance
- It's placed at the root level to track all navigation within the app
- Both admin mode and normal mode are covered by the Analytics integration
- No configuration options were needed - the component works with default settings
- The integration follows Vercel's recommended best practices for React applications
